TITLE:: Pkuramoto
SUMMARY:: Experimental dense coupled phase integration
CATEGORIES:: Streams-Patterns-Events>Patterns>Patternarium
RELATED:: Classes/ProtationWord, Classes/Pscan, Guides/Patternarium-Systems

DESCRIPTION::
Experimental: this API may change before 1.0.

Integrates d(theta[i])/dt = frequencies[i] + sum_j coupling[i][j] * sin(theta[j]-theta[i]) / N. Frequencies are angular radians per time unit. For cycles per unit time, multiply by 2pi. Scalar coupling fills the entire matrix; a uniform matrix therefore agrees with that scalar. Matrix rows receive influence from columns. Signed coupling and frequencies are permitted.

The default fixed-step method is classical RK4; Euler is also available for comparison. No automatic adaptive-step or numerical-error guarantee is provided. Small steps relative to natural rotation and coupling are recommended. Dense integration costs O(N squared) per step, with at most 128 oscillators. Initial phases default to thread-RNG uniform values in [0,2pi), reproducible with Pseed.

The first output is after one integration step. Length counts integration steps, including filtered steps in wraps mode. Phases are normalized to [0,2pi). Wraps are signed cycle-crossing counts derived from unwrapped advancement, including multiple crossings in one step. Negative rotation from phase zero counts a negative wrap on entering the previous cycle. No individual crossing time is interpolated inside a step.

State output is a fresh Event containing time, phases, wraps and order. The order magnitude is abs(mean(exp(i*theta))), bounded to [0,1] for floating roundoff. Phases yields fresh phase Arrays, order yields only the magnitude, and wraps emits state Events only for steps with a nonzero wrap count. An exactly stationary phase vector ends wraps mode immediately, since no future crossing is possible. More than 100000 consecutive silent integration steps in wraps mode throws, preventing a stationary infinite stream from blocking next forever. Time, advancement, wrap-count and output-index overflow are guarded. State is local to the stream; outputs never expose internal phase Arrays.

CLASSMETHODS::
METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: frequencies
Nonempty collection of 1..128 finite angular frequencies; evaluated once.
ARGUMENT:: coupling
Finite scalar (default 1) or square finite matrix, evaluated once.
ARGUMENT:: phases
Nil for random initial phases, or a same-size finite phase collection; evaluated once.
ARGUMENT:: step
Strictly positive finite integration step, default 0.01; sampled once.
ARGUMENT:: length
Nonnegative Integer or inf, default inf; sampled once.
ARGUMENT:: method
rk4 (default) or euler; sampled once.
ARGUMENT:: output
state (default), phases, order or wraps; sampled once. Once-evaluated arguments accept literals, Functions or Patterns yielding the required value.

INSTANCEMETHODS::
METHOD:: storeArgs
Returns constructor arguments in public constructor order.
METHOD:: embedInStream
Yields values and returns the latest inval when the stream ends.

EXAMPLES::
code::
Pkuramoto([1, 2], 0, [0, 0], 0.1, 4).asStream.all;
::

Phases become chord voices; synchronization magnitude becomes filter brightness. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Pkuramoto / Value stream
var values = {
Pkuramoto([1, 2], 0, [0, 0], 0.1, 4).asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \saw, degree: if(x.isKindOf(Dictionary)) { (x[\phases]/2pi*7).round } { if(x.isArray) { (x/2pi*7).round } { 0 } }, cutoff: if(x.isNumber) { x.linexp(0,1,300,6000) } { 1800 }, dur: 0.1, amp: 0.045)
}.play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Musical example
Load the main Guide example instruments first.
code::
(
Pbind(\instrument, \saw, \degree, 0,
    \network, Pkuramoto([6.1, 6.3, 6.5], 2, [0, 2, 4], 0.05, 64),
    \cutoff, Pfunc { |e| e[\network][\order].linexp(0, 1, 400, 6000) },
    \dur, 0.05).play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Independent polyrhythms
code::
Pkuramoto(2pi * [1, 1.5], 0, [0, 0], 0.05, 40, output: \wraps).asStream.all;
::

Phases become chord voices; synchronization magnitude becomes filter brightness. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Pkuramoto / Independent polyrhythms
var values = {
Pkuramoto(2pi * [1, 1.5], 0, [0, 0], 0.05, 40, output: \wraps).asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \saw, degree: if(x.isKindOf(Dictionary)) { (x[\phases]/2pi*7).round } { if(x.isArray) { (x/2pi*7).round } { 0 } }, cutoff: if(x.isNumber) { x.linexp(0,1,300,6000) } { 1800 }, dur: 0.1, amp: 0.045)
}.play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Synchronization as coupling increases
code::
[0, 1, 4].collect { |k|
    Pkuramoto([1, 1.1, 0.9], k, [0, 2, 4], 0.05, 100, output: \order).asStream.all.last
};
::

Phases become chord voices; synchronization magnitude becomes filter brightness. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Pkuramoto / Synchronization as coupling increases
var values = {
[0, 1, 4].collect { |k|
    Pkuramoto([1, 1.1, 0.9], k, [0, 2, 4], 0.05, 100, output: \order).asStream.all.last
};
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \saw, degree: if(x.isKindOf(Dictionary)) { (x[\phases]/2pi*7).round } { if(x.isArray) { (x/2pi*7).round } { 0 } }, cutoff: if(x.isNumber) { x.linexp(0,1,300,6000) } { 1800 }, dur: 0.1, amp: 0.045)
}.play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Divergent frequencies
code::
Pkuramoto([1, 3, 6], 0.1, [0, 0, 0], 0.05, 50, output: \order).asStream.all;
::

Phases become chord voices; synchronization magnitude becomes filter brightness. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Pkuramoto / Divergent frequencies
var values = {
Pkuramoto([1, 3, 6], 0.1, [0, 0, 0], 0.05, 50, output: \order).asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \saw, degree: if(x.isKindOf(Dictionary)) { (x[\phases]/2pi*7).round } { if(x.isArray) { (x/2pi*7).round } { 0 } }, cutoff: if(x.isNumber) { x.linexp(0,1,300,6000) } { 1800 }, dur: 0.1, amp: 0.045)
}.play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Phase clusters with a matrix
code::
Pkuramoto([1, 1, 1, 1], [[4,4,0,0], [4,4,0,0], [0,0,4,4], [0,0,4,4]],
    [0, 0.1, pi, pi+0.1], 0.05, 32, output: \phases).asStream.all;
::

Phases become chord voices; synchronization magnitude becomes filter brightness. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Pkuramoto / Phase clusters with a matrix
var values = {
Pkuramoto([1, 1, 1, 1], [[4,4,0,0], [4,4,0,0], [0,0,4,4], [0,0,4,4]],
    [0, 0.1, pi, pi+0.1], 0.05, 32, output: \phases).asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \saw, degree: if(x.isKindOf(Dictionary)) { (x[\phases]/2pi*7).round } { if(x.isArray) { (x/2pi*7).round } { 0 } }, cutoff: if(x.isNumber) { x.linexp(0,1,300,6000) } { 1800 }, dur: 0.1, amp: 0.045)
}.play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Triggering notes at wraps
code::
(
Pbind(\instrument, \mallet,
    \network, Pkuramoto(2pi * [2, 3], 0.2, [0, 0], 0.05, 80),
    \type, Pfunc { |e| if(e[\network][\wraps].any { |x| x != 0 }) { \note } { \rest } },
    \degree, Pfunc { |e| if(e[\network][\wraps][0] > 0) { 0 } { 7 } },
    \dur, 0.05).play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Order parameter as a synthesis control
code::
Pkuramoto([6.1, 6.3, 6.5], 2, [0, 2, 4], 0.05, 32, output: \order).collect { |r| (cutoff: r.linexp(0, 1, 400, 6000)) }.asStream.all;
::

Pitch follows the output; repeated phrases make the structure audible. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Pkuramoto / Order parameter as a synthesis control
var values = {
Pkuramoto([6.1, 6.3, 6.5], 2, [0, 2, 4], 0.05, 32, output: \order).collect { |r| (cutoff: r.linexp(0, 1, 400, 6000)) }.asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    x.copy.putAll((instrument: \saw, degree: 0, dur: 0.1, amp: 0.07))
}.play;
)
::
